utathione  reduced glutathione pool have to be  regenerated and from oxidized  glutathione to reduce glutathione  this conversion is facilitated by  glutathione reductase so glutathione  reductase actually reduces oxidized  glutathione to reduce glutathione with  the help of nadph which in turn was  produced in the  pentose phosphate pathway that is why  pentose phosphate pathway in our body is  also very important  and apart from these glutam peroxidase  and glutathione reductase another  important enzyme is catalyst when the  amount of hydrogen peroxide  is high  then catalyze also  helps to convert h2o2  to  h2o that means peroxide to water and in  this respect sod  glutathione peroxidase glutathiones and  catalase  acts together to combat ross in a  in our cell so these are all enzymatic  scavenger of ross  now we would talk a bit about  non-enzymatic scavenger of ross  and we would see how  non-enzymatic scavenger of ross  functions inside our cell  so first non-enzymatic scavenger is  chelating agent such as edta so edta  actually chelates the ross  and  reduce its harmful effect apart from  edta there is vitamin e alpha tocopherol  so alpha tocopherol has a hydroxyl group  and say the alpha tocopherol can uh  break chains  of peroxides so let's say lipid  peroxidation already took place and this  alpha tocopherol has a hydrogen hydroxyl  group and now  it could react with that peroxidized  lipid  and it could form a alpha tocopherol  radical  and hydroxy peroxide radical would be  produced so this alpha tocopherol  radical  it's actually a free radical but it's  stable so it won't create another free  radical and it won't  evoke the chain reaction  in this way vitamin e acts as a very  efficient chain breaking antioxidant in  our tissues and help to help to protect  the polyunsaturated fatty acids of our  biomembrane apart from vitamin e vitamin  c which is available from all kind of  citrus fruit is also a very good  antioxidant  and vitamin a which is retinol which is  found in mainly carrots and other  sources also have to some extent  antioxidant activity  so with the help of enzyme scavengers  and non-enzymatic scavengers of ross our  body tries to combat with  react these harmful reactive oxygen  species and try to save our body  and i hope you enjoyed this video please  give it a quick thumbs up  and please subscribe  thank you

